# Example PAM integration for goodixfpd — do NOT copy blindly.
# See docs/pam-integration.md for the safe procedure (sudo first, then login, never a lockout).
#
# The fingerprint is an ADDITIONAL 'sufficient' factor: if the sensor accepts, auth passes;
# if it fails or the daemon is not there, PAM GOES ON with the password (pam_unix line below).
# NEVER use 'required' alone for the fingerprint: it would lock the user out.
#
# --- /etc/pam.d/sudo (example, at the top of the auth stack) ---
#
#   auth  sufficient  pam_exec.so  quiet  /usr/local/lib/goodixfp/goodixfp-verify
#   auth  include     system-auth          # <- the existing password stack (fallback)
#
# pam_exec passes the user in PAM_USER; the client exits 0 on recognition, 1 otherwise.
# 'quiet' silences the client's output in PAM (the "Touch the sensor" prompt stays on stderr).
